Q: How to get rid of this error in React native A: <p>This warning is usually not about an actual visible period in your code. React Native does not allow raw text nodes inside a <code>&lt;View&gt;</code>, and it treats pretty much anything printable as text. That includes spaces, newlines, string fragments, conditional strings etc and even some strings returned by third party components.</p>
<p>Some common examples:</p>
<pre class="lang-jsx prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;View&gt;
  {&quot; &quot;}
&lt;/View&gt;
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-jsx prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;View&gt;
  {loading &amp;&amp; &quot;.&quot;}
&lt;/View&gt;
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-jsx prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;View&gt;
  &lt;&gt;
    .
  &lt;/&gt;
&lt;/View&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>If you’re stuck, one practical way to hunt it down is to temporarily comment out suspicious components only and uncomment them one by one. It’s a bit of a pain, but it makes it easier to spot which subtree is returning the stray text. If it turns out not to be your code, it’s likely coming from a library somewhere in the render chain.</p>
<p>If you want to post the component or a minimal repro, I can take a look and help narrow it down.</p>

Q: Draw a rectangle on the corner of the TCalendarView items A: <p><code>CalendarViewViewInfo.DoDrawItem</code> was not the correct approach, because it was calling the <code>DrawDayItem</code> event, resulting in a stack overflow.</p>
<p>I want to thank @RemyLebeau for showing me how to address the Calendar's internal drawer instead of creating a second one. His solution works like a charm:</p>
<pre class="lang-pascal prettyprint-override"><code>procedure TfrmPreparation_order_Workload.CalendarDrawDayItem(Sender: TObject; DrawParams: TDrawViewInfoParams; CalendarViewViewInfo: TCellItemViewInfo);
var
  procedure DrawTriangle(ARectangle: TRect; ACanvas: TCanvas);
  var
    APoints: array [0..2] of TPoint;
  begin
    APoints[0] := ARectangle.Location;
    APoints[1] := Point(ARectangle.Location.x + 7, ARectangle.Location.y);
    APoints[2] := Point(ARectangle.Location.x, ARectangle.Location.y + 7);

    ACanvas.Pen.Color := clNavy;
    ACanvas.Brush.Color := clNavy;
    ACanvas.Polygon(APoints);
  end;
begin
  if Odd(CalendarViewViewInfo.Date.Day) then
  begin
    Calendar.NeedCurrentViewInfo.Controller.Drawer.DrawCalendarItem(DrawParams, DrawParams.Canvas, CalendarViewViewInfo);
    DrawTriangle(DrawParams.DrawRect, DrawParams.Canvas);
    DrawParams.Handled := True;
  end;
end;
</code></pre>
